    crm:P183i_has_representation <https://ids.lib.harvard.edu/ids/iiif/493338094/full/full/0/default.jpg> ;
    rdf:value """Friday, May 8, 1908
Train to Messina 
Fine.
I was in bed all day with my “poisoning”. I felt horribly weak and headachey and packing was torture. However, I got it done by bits, and we left by the 7.20 train with Placci. The night was  horrible .
Bernhard took Placci, the Princess Candriano to the gallery and returned to lunch with her, Ethel joining them. The Princess said privately that she was delighted to have that chance of rendering hospitality to Ethel without involving any Neapolitans, for Ethel (partly on account of her liaison with the Duca d’Aosta) is no more a persona grata in Neapolitan society. Bernhard was shocked, for Ethel had told him that the Princess Candriano was her best friend!"""^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 151 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1908> .

